# Build context for the mcos-shell image (Dockerfile.node, context `.`).
#
# Why this file exists: Dockerfile.node does `COPY . .`, so without it the shell
# image baked the gitignored root `.env` — live ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and
# VOYAGE_API_KEY — plus the host's Windows node_modules, a stale .next, .git and
# every sub-app's source. CI was never exposed (actions/checkout carries no
# .env), but any local `docker build` was. Audit finding [HIGH], 2026-08-04.
#
# Safe to exclude apps/ here: this is the ONLY build using context `.`. OCHI,
# Penny Post and Scout each build from their own directory (see the CI matrix in
# .github/workflows/docker-publish.yml and the compose build contexts), so their
# sources are unaffected by this file.

# Secrets — the reason this file exists. Never relax without re-reading the above.
.env
.env.*
!.env*.example

# Host build artifacts (Windows-native binaries would break the Linux image)
node_modules
.next
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
build_output.log

# VCS + tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
.claude
.vscode

# Sub-apps build from their own contexts, never from this one
apps

# Docs, design scratch and compose files are not inputs to the shell build
docs
*.md
!README.md
docker-compose*.yml
Dockerfile
Dockerfile.*
!Dockerfile.node
nginx.conf
# Untracked local scratch (gitignored, so CI never sees it — this line keeps
# LOCAL builds equally clean; found riding into the image at the review gate)
draft_issues*.js

# ⚠️ public/brain.json is NOT excluded, deliberately.
# It is Hoot's RAG index and is read at RUNTIME, not just at build:
# src/lib/brain.ts:27 resolves it via process.cwd() on every knowledge lookup.
# Excluding it produces an image that boots fine and then answers every question
# with no knowledge ("brain.json not found"), which is worse than a hard failure
# because nothing crashes. The 2026-08-04 audit's suggested exclude list named
# this file; that recommendation is wrong and this comment is here so the next
# person does not re-apply it.
#
# 🔴 KNOWN, UNFIXED (found 2026-08-04): the PUBLISHED image does not contain
# brain.json anyway, and this file is not the reason. `.gitignore:45` ignores
# public/brain.json, so it is untracked; CI builds from actions/checkout, which
# carries only tracked files; and Dockerfile.node never runs `npm run ingest`.
# So ghcr.io/…/mcos-shell has always shipped without a knowledge base and
# production Hoot answers from the model alone. Keeping it un-excluded here fixes
# LOCAL docker builds only. The real fix is a decision for Ernest — commit the
# artifact, generate it in CI with VOYAGE_API_KEY from secrets, or mount it on the
# VPS — so do not "fix" it by editing this file. Once the shell's /health route is
# deployed, `curl https://mechanicalcupcakes.fun/health` reports
# {"knowledge":"missing"} and will flip to "loaded" when it is genuinely solved.
